n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡t|=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\ge 0$ when $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{5}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{sin}^{2}⁡t}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{25{sin}^{2}⁡t}{5} \\\\  & =5{sin}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}5{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =25{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =25{\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =25\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =25(\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330480 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330481 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330482 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330483 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330484 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1041 "selection" 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330482 13194139535087 true] [17592186330479 1110 #uuid "6f98bb9d-7cd2-51d1-bc92-804e8c3bc811" 13194139535087 true] [17592186330480 1034 "\\frac{20}{3}" 13194139535087 true] [17592186330480 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535087 true] [17592186330480 1111 #uuid "f93a92a5-7142-5e27-98a4-94f99cb7ca17" 13194139535087 true] [17592186330481 1034 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139535087 true] [17592186330481